SRS.md:38:| SRS-01 | The flake exports `nixosModules.aws-pvm-host` and a downstream `nixosSystem` can evaluate with that module in `modules = [ ... ]`. | SCOPE-01 | FR-01 | manual |\r\n.keel/epics/VFhLhfrqk/voyages/VFhLjViAG/SRS.md:39:| SRS-02 | Port exports a companion `firecracker-pvm-host-kit` package/metadata surface whose package identity, host-kernel release, Firecracker build, binary name/env, and boot args match the canonical AWS x86_64 PVM host-kit contract. | SCOPE-02 | FR-02 | manual |\r\n.keel/epics/VFhLhfrqk/PRD.md:16:| GOAL-01 | Downstream infrastructure can consume Port's AWS PVM host contract as a first-class flake export instead of an out-of-band module file invented in another repo. | A downstream `nixosSystem` evaluates with `port.nixosModules.aws-pvm-host` as an imported module. | One clean downstream module import proof |\r\n.keel/epics/VFhLhfrqk/PRD.md:37:- [SCOPE-04] AWS VM Import/Export automation, S3 upload/import orchestration, and AMI publication policy.\r\n.keel/epics/VFhLhfrqk/PRD.md:38:- [SCOPE-05] Downstream bootstrap, IAM, DNS, scheduler, or GitOps orchestration.\r\n.keel/epics/VFhLhfrqk/PRD.md:39:- [SCOPE-06] Generalizing the exported surface to arm64, GCP, Azure, or a broader host taxonomy.\r\n.keel/epics/VFhLhfrqk/PRD.md:48:| FR-01 | Export `port.nixosModules.aws-pvm-host` as a downstream-consumable module that can be imported by `nixosSystem`. | GOAL-01 | must | This is the minimum first-class flake surface requested by downstream consumers. |\r\nwebsite/docs/path-to-production/aws.mdx:57:- `port.nixosModules.aws-pvm-host`\r\nwebsite/docs/path-to-production/aws.mdx:58:- `port.packages.x86_64-linux.firecracker-pvm-host-kit`\r\nwebsite/docs/path-to-production/aws.mdx:72:  --override-input port path:/absolute/path/to/port\r\nwebsite/docs/path-to-production/aws.mdx:92:  --package-name firecracker-pvm-host-kit \\\r\nwebsite/docs/path-to-production/aws.mdx:139:It does **not** mean that Port already ships EC2 provisioning, IAM, VPC wiring,\r\nwebsite/docs/path-to-production/aws.mdx:140:DNS, autoscaling, or a broad multi-provider PVM abstraction layer.\r\nwebsite/docs/path-to-production/aws.mdx:149:- arm64 Firecracker/PVM remains research-only\r\ndocs/aws.md:26:| Hosted Firecracker `pvm` on `x86_64` | Hardening a provider-specific AWS deployment path around a prepared node and no-fallback runtime contract | prepared AWS host kit, dedicated PVM artifacts, imported ready PVM lane, hosted control plane, node agent | EC2 provisioning, IAM, VPC, DNS, or a generic multi-provider promise |\r\ndocs/aws.md:64:- `port.nixosModules.aws-pvm-host`\r\ndocs/aws.md:65:- `port.packages.x86_64-linux.firecracker-pvm-host-kit`\r\ndocs/aws.md:84:        port.nixosModules.aws-pvm-host\r\ndocs/aws.md:139:### Downstream AMI Handoff\r\ndocs/aws.md:151:`port.nixosModules.aws-pvm-host` surface directly:\r\ndocs/aws.md:162:  --override-input port path:/absolute/path/to/port\r\ndocs/aws.md:169:- downstream `infra` owns AMI build, upload, VM Import/Export, publication, and\r\ndocs/aws.md:194:PORT_DEMO_TOKEN=demo-token port --config /tmp/port-aws-pvm.toml control-plane prepare-pvm-node --control-plane demo --node aws-linux-node --architecture x86-64 --provenance repo-proof --package-name firecracker-pvm-host-kit --package-version 2026.03 --host-kernel-release 6.12.0-port-pvm --firecracker-build v1.12.0-port-pvm\r\ndocs/aws.md:228:- accidental documentation drift that turns arm64 Firecracker/PVM into an\r\ndocs/aws.md:247:- IAM setup\r\ndocs/aws.md:249:- DNS management\r\ndocs/aws.md:258:- arm64 Firecracker/PVM remains research-only\r\nREADME.md:52:- the Port flake now exports `nixosModules.aws-pvm-host` and\r\nREADME.md:53:  `packages.x86_64-linux.firecracker-pvm-host-kit` as the supported downstream\r\nREADME.md:55:- Port still does not claim EC2 provisioning, IAM, VPC wiring, DNS, or arm64\r\nrun-parts: unrecognized option '--regex'\r\nBusyBox v1.37.0 () multi-call binary.\r\n\r\nUsage: run-parts [-a ARG]... [-u UMASK] [--rever